# Comma-separated exact IPs or CIDRs allowed to supply X-Forwarded-For and
# X-Real-IP. Empty means the gateway trusts no forwarding headers — so the client
# address is always the peer, which behind a frontend hop is the frontend's own
# pod, and every rate-limit bucket collapses onto it.
#
# A DEPLOYED gateway therefore refuses to start on an empty value: a cell's
# ingress and frontend reach the gateway from known ranges, and naming them is
# what makes the anonymous and authentication-factor budgets per-client rather
# than per-cell. Empty is correct here and only here, where the peer IS the client.
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=

# Protected waypoint identity. Required outside native development; the cell
# supplies and pins it together with workload-port enrollment and HTTP policy.
WORKLOAD_PRESENTER_PRINCIPAL=

# What one caller may ask of the gateway in a minute: a signed-in person within
# their organization, or an anonymous client address. Empty means 1000. A 20%
# burst is allowed above it.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_PERSON_PER_MINUTE=

# The ceiling everyone in one organization counts under together, above their
# own budgets, so no number of members lets one organization take the gateway
# from the others. Empty means 20000, with the same 20% burst. A value below the
# per-person budget fails the boot.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_ORGANIZATION_PER_MINUTE=
